WEBVTT

00:00:00.411 --> 00:00:05.045
Last updated: 29 September 20 26

00:00:06.008 --> 00:00:08.168
The short version.

00:00:08.923 --> 00:00:11.606
Ordinary Lolly editing, rendering and

00:00:11.665 --> 00:00:14.441
downloads happen on your device and need

00:00:14.499 --> 00:00:15.920
no account.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.889
Features such as sharing, Sync, hosted

00:00:19.975 --> 00:00:22.062
rendering and optional lolly-work

00:00:22.124 --> 00:00:25.511
organisation services send the data they

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:28.150
need to the destination you or your

00:00:28.215 --> 00:00:30.195
organisation use.

00:00:30.992 --> 00:00:33.715
lolly-work can hold shared content,

00:00:33.796 --> 00:00:36.926
identities, audit records and configured

00:00:36.987 --> 00:00:38.819
usage telemetry.

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:42.715
The sections below distinguish local data

00:00:42.869 --> 00:00:45.769
from those server-held records.

00:00:46.909 --> 00:00:49.393
What this policy covers

00:00:50.358 --> 00:00:53.709
Lolly is open-source software - an engine,

00:00:53.796 --> 00:00:56.670
several app shells «web, desktop, mobile,

00:00:56.748 --> 00:00:59.646
CLI» and a browser extension - that anyone

00:00:59.706 --> 00:01:00.995
can run.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:04.619
This policy has two parts:

00:01:05.384 --> 00:01:08.068
The software itself: what it does and

00:01:08.118 --> 00:01:10.944
doesn't do with your data, wherever it

00:01:11.916 --> 00:01:13.167
runs.

00:01:13.941 --> 00:01:16.889
This is a property of the code, so it's

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:19.909
true of every Lolly deployment, ours or

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.619
anyone else's.

00:01:22.411 --> 00:01:25.295
lolly-tools, the reference deployment SUSE

00:01:25.375 --> 00:01:28.221
operates: the specific choices

00:01:29.144 --> 00:01:31.543
made running its optional server-side

00:01:31.603 --> 00:01:34.503
pieces «what's logged, for how long, by

00:01:34.563 --> 00:01:35.545
whom».

00:01:36.298 --> 00:01:38.369
If you're using a self-hosted or

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.980
enterprise Lolly instance, the software

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:43.695
behaviour below still applies, but the

00:01:43.762 --> 00:01:46.318
operator of that instance - not SUSE - is

00:01:46.363 --> 00:01:49.319
responsible for anything server-side:

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.387
their render endpoint, their MCP server,

00:01:52.447 --> 00:01:54.482
their Content Credentials certificate

00:01:54.542 --> 00:01:56.756
authority and their optional lolly-work

00:01:56.792 --> 00:01:59.742
instance, including its accounts, shared

00:01:59.802 --> 00:02:03.045
content, telemetry and audit records.

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:06.968
Ask them for their own policy.

00:02:07.766 --> 00:02:10.539
See Adoption & Governance for what

00:02:10.615 --> 00:02:13.068
operating Lolly involves.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.175
The app: what stays on your device

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:21.322
Lolly's web, desktop and mobile shells run

00:02:21.381 --> 00:02:24.869
the entire render engine client-side.

00:02:25.632 --> 00:02:28.314
The local render and download path needs

00:02:28.376 --> 00:02:31.491
no server once its tools, assets and

00:02:31.547 --> 00:02:33.820
encoders are available.

00:02:34.571 --> 00:02:37.174
Connected organisation workflows can

00:02:37.294 --> 00:02:39.824
separately save shared state or submit

00:02:39.884 --> 00:02:42.791
content for review and delivery, as

00:02:42.851 --> 00:02:44.695
described below.

00:02:45.477 --> 00:02:48.894
Standalone app use sets no cookies.

00:02:49.663 --> 00:02:52.565
Organisation sign-in and optional CA

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:55.594
enrolment have separate cookies, described

00:02:55.655 --> 00:02:56.819
below.

00:02:57.585 --> 00:03:00.249
The app keeps these local records;

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.455
sharing, Sync and organisation workflows

00:03:03.531 --> 00:03:05.820
are separate data flows:

00:03:06.572 --> 00:03:09.276
Interface preferences - theme, language,

00:03:09.337 --> 00:03:12.174
sound settings, sidebar/zoom

00:03:13.087 --> 00:03:15.748
sizing, sort and view choices, which

00:03:15.839 --> 00:03:17.706
onboarding tips you've seen - in

00:03:17.766 --> 00:03:20.871
localStorage, so they're available before

00:03:20.931 --> 00:03:23.295
the app has finished booting.

00:03:24.079 --> 00:03:27.165
An offline cache of the tool catalogue and

00:03:27.238 --> 00:03:30.086
asset previews, so the gallery

00:03:31.015 --> 00:03:33.718
works without a connection.

00:03:34.509 --> 00:03:37.405
Local usage counters for your profile

00:03:37.472 --> 00:03:40.555
card's stats «how many exports, which

00:03:41.486 --> 00:03:43.770
tools» - a small bounded blob in

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:47.441
localStorage, never read by us, never sent

00:03:47.509 --> 00:03:48.719
anywhere.

00:03:49.506 --> 00:03:51.900
Your own documents, saved sessions,

00:03:51.959 --> 00:03:54.984
uploaded assets and fonts - stored in

00:03:55.875 --> 00:03:59.093
IndexedDB on your device.

00:03:59.862 --> 00:04:02.158
Personal saves stay there unless you

00:04:02.221 --> 00:04:05.604
choose Sync or sharing; organisation-held

00:04:05.693 --> 00:04:09.418
sessions and assets are described below.

00:04:10.199 --> 00:04:13.235
Local storage itself sends none of these

00:04:13.296 --> 00:04:15.194
records to us.

00:04:15.952 --> 00:04:18.514
Optional network features have their own

00:04:18.575 --> 00:04:21.754
destinations and data handling, described

00:04:21.815 --> 00:04:22.970
below.

00:04:23.739 --> 00:04:25.907
Clearing the site's storage in your

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:28.800
browser removes the local copy at any

00:04:28.872 --> 00:04:33.577
time, and so does Settings → Storage →

00:04:33.653 --> 00:04:36.894
Clear all my data, which also turns off

00:04:36.984 --> 00:04:38.469
Sync first.

00:04:39.254 --> 00:04:43.118
«Under the ePrivacy Directive Art.

00:04:43.894 --> 00:04:47.081
5«3», storage that is strictly necessary

00:04:47.208 --> 00:04:49.929
for the service you asked for doesn't

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:53.482
require consent - only transparency, which

00:04:53.544 --> 00:04:55.851
is what this document and the in-app

00:04:55.925 --> 00:04:57.844
notice both are.»

00:04:58.639 --> 00:05:01.247
Your own backup of this data - the

00:05:01.331 --> 00:05:04.365
lolly-backup bundle produced by Export my

00:05:04.427 --> 00:05:08.469
data - is a file you keep and control.

00:05:09.216 --> 00:05:11.934
It never touches our servers unless you

00:05:11.996 --> 00:05:15.094
choose to send it somewhere yourself.

00:05:15.894 --> 00:05:18.443
See Data Transfer.

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:22.092
On-device utilities

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:25.960
Some tools - Strip Hidden Data, Compress

00:05:26.044 --> 00:05:29.115
PDF and others carrying the "Runs on your

00:05:29.173 --> 00:05:32.017
device" badge - operate on a file you

00:05:32.073 --> 00:05:33.320
provide.

00:05:34.094 --> 00:05:36.587
The file is read into memory in your

00:05:36.649 --> 00:05:39.804
browser, transformed locally and offered

00:05:39.866 --> 00:05:42.044
back as a download.

00:05:42.795 --> 00:05:45.536
It is never uploaded, because there is no

00:05:45.656 --> 00:05:49.094
server in the path to upload it to.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.787
These utilities work offline, and their

00:05:52.875 --> 00:05:56.298
output carries no watermark or metadata of

00:05:56.393 --> 00:05:59.219
ours - the point of most of them is to

00:05:59.279 --> 00:06:03.119
remove & protect data, not add risk.

00:06:03.868 --> 00:06:07.077
Prepare for sharing holds working inputs,

00:06:07.139 --> 00:06:09.664
private findings and replacement maps in

00:06:09.724 --> 00:06:12.613
memory, without automatically adding them

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:15.920
to history, links, backups or sync.

00:06:16.695 --> 00:06:19.514
Inspection and replacement do not send

00:06:19.596 --> 00:06:22.767
file contents to a server or validate

00:06:22.829 --> 00:06:24.869
credentials online.

00:06:25.655 --> 00:06:28.399
Users choose whether to copy, download,

00:06:28.482 --> 00:06:31.624
send or explicitly save a result to their

00:06:31.685 --> 00:06:34.806
library; a saved result then follows

00:06:34.901 --> 00:06:38.344
normal library backup and sync settings.

00:06:39.131 --> 00:06:42.217
Recipe files omit prior payloads and

00:06:42.278 --> 00:06:44.019
literal mappings.

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:48.176
Summary reports contain counts, scope ID'S

00:06:48.223 --> 00:06:49.994
and file hashes.

00:06:50.766 --> 00:06:53.773
The CLI can also save a private review

00:06:53.859 --> 00:06:57.491
file containing original values, only when

00:06:57.561 --> 00:07:00.969
explicitly requested with --review-file.

00:07:01.744 --> 00:07:04.709
Clearing or leaving a browser preparation

00:07:04.791 --> 00:07:08.370
view releases its working state; this is

00:07:08.439 --> 00:07:11.405
not a promise of forensic erasure from

00:07:11.468 --> 00:07:14.194
browser or OS memory.

00:07:15.319 --> 00:07:18.526
Every network request the app can make

00:07:19.547 --> 00:07:22.348
The table below lists the app's network

00:07:22.411 --> 00:07:23.668
features.

00:07:24.425 --> 00:07:27.525
Organisation services are grouped in one

00:07:27.585 --> 00:07:30.720
row and detailed in their own section.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:34.484
An operator's configured identity and

00:07:34.578 --> 00:07:38.060
asset providers can add destinations to

00:07:38.122 --> 00:07:39.769
that deployment.

00:07:40.539 --> 00:07:43.638
Every fixed host in that table is also the

00:07:43.699 --> 00:07:45.794
complete allowlist in the app's

00:07:45.856 --> 00:07:49.116
Content-Security-Policy, which the browser

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:50.694
enforces.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:54.324
So the list is not only a description of

00:07:54.385 --> 00:07:57.012
what the code does today, it is the

00:07:57.092 --> 00:08:00.495
boundary the browser holds the app to: a

00:08:00.582 --> 00:08:03.356
future change that tried to contact some

00:08:03.392 --> 00:08:06.167
other host would be blocked, not silently

00:08:06.227 --> 00:08:07.445
permitted.

00:08:08.235 --> 00:08:11.189
One row is the deliberate exception, and

00:08:11.252 --> 00:08:14.834
its own cell explains it: Send to LinkedIn

00:08:14.877 --> 00:08:18.054
exists in the desktop apps only, and the

00:08:18.144 --> 00:08:20.658
web app's policy lists neither of its

00:08:20.719 --> 00:08:23.214
hosts - the web app could not reach them

00:08:23.318 --> 00:08:25.769
even if its code tried.

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.321
Two more rows, Bluesky and Discord, are

00:08:29.394 --> 00:08:32.703
desktop-only the same way, and their hosts

00:08:32.791 --> 00:08:35.242
are left out of the web policy for the

00:08:35.333 --> 00:08:36.770
same reason.

00:08:37.546 --> 00:08:40.294
Five rows have no fixed host, because you

00:08:40.354 --> 00:08:43.401
choose the address at the moment of use: a

00:08:43.461 --> 00:08:46.955
URL you ask a tool to capture, a remote

00:08:47.016 --> 00:08:49.433
instance you point the shell at, and your

00:08:49.499 --> 00:08:53.170
own Mastodon server, WebDAV server or S3

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:56.845
bucket «the last two also as a sync home».

00:08:57.652 --> 00:09:00.931
None of those is in the policy, and each

00:09:00.994 --> 00:09:04.169
uses the destination you selected.

00:09:04.935 --> 00:09:08.210
A lolly-work deployment must also permit

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:11.035
its configured identity providers and

00:09:11.127 --> 00:09:14.375
service connections; it does not inherit

00:09:14.467 --> 00:09:17.162
an unchanging list of public-reference

00:09:17.222 --> 00:09:18.370
hosts.

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:21.859
The Penpot row reaches Penpot through the

00:09:21.951 --> 00:09:25.218
app's own origin, so it is covered by

00:09:25.314 --> 00:09:26.369
'self'.

00:09:27.136 --> 00:09:29.390
A deployment that wants none of the

00:09:29.479 --> 00:09:32.349
optional ones «an enterprise instance with

00:09:32.406 --> 00:09:35.778
its own fonts, say» removes those hosts

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:38.738
from its policy and the features fail

00:09:38.823 --> 00:09:41.544
closed rather than reaching out.

00:09:42.317 --> 00:09:45.266
Most fetches bring tools, fonts or models

00:09:45.358 --> 00:09:47.070
to your device.

00:09:47.857 --> 00:09:51.200
Send actions transmit the selected file,

00:09:51.268 --> 00:09:54.116
personal Sync transmits a backup to your

00:09:54.177 --> 00:09:57.967
chosen storage, and organisation services

00:09:58.035 --> 00:10:00.927
transmit the content or metadata needed

00:10:01.029 --> 00:10:02.794
for shared work.

00:10:03.563 --> 00:10:07.344
Hosted render and MCP requests have the

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:10.694
separate data flows described below.

00:10:11.472 --> 00:10:14.668
A note on what we removed.

00:10:15.444 --> 00:10:18.810
Verify can check SEAL signatures, a scheme

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:21.686
where a file's signing key is published in

00:10:21.748 --> 00:10:23.069
DNS.

00:10:23.832 --> 00:10:27.406
Browsers can't make DNS queries, so any

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:30.250
web implementation has to route the lookup

00:10:30.344 --> 00:10:33.682
through a third-party DNS-over-HTTPS

00:10:33.742 --> 00:10:36.594
resolver - which would show that operator

00:10:36.655 --> 00:10:39.391
the domain being checked plus your IP

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:40.619
address.

00:10:41.425 --> 00:10:44.567
We used to use Cloudflare's.

00:10:45.333 --> 00:10:47.427
We don't any more, and there is no

00:10:47.483 --> 00:10:50.538
replacement: the web app now passes no

00:10:50.598 --> 00:10:53.869
resolver at all, so SEAL verification here

00:10:53.929 --> 00:10:56.595
makes zero network requests.

00:10:57.375 --> 00:11:00.267
Files whose SEAL record carries its key

00:11:00.331 --> 00:11:04.068
inline still verify completely offline.

00:11:04.838 --> 00:11:08.165
Files whose key lives in DNS report "no

00:11:08.253 --> 00:11:11.269
key resolver" instead, and you can check

00:11:11.329 --> 00:11:14.601
those in the desktop or command-line app,

00:11:14.658 --> 00:11:17.417
which resolve DNS natively through your

00:11:17.481 --> 00:11:20.995
own machine with no third party involved.

00:11:21.778 --> 00:11:24.693
You can confirm this yourself: greppable

00:11:24.755 --> 00:11:27.300
checks for this and every other claim on

00:11:27.346 --> 00:11:30.382
this page, with the exact commands and

00:11:30.437 --> 00:11:33.471
expected output, live at Verify It

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:34.769
Yourself.

00:11:35.909 --> 00:11:39.708
Organisation services with lolly-work

00:11:40.732 --> 00:11:43.118
lolly-work is the Lolly project's

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:46.271
optional, separately deployed organisation

00:11:46.349 --> 00:11:47.494
service.

00:11:48.251 --> 00:11:51.119
Connecting to an instance introduces

00:11:51.234 --> 00:11:55.194
server-held data alongside local editing.

00:11:55.946 --> 00:11:58.736
Its operator is responsible for that

00:11:58.794 --> 00:12:01.622
deployment's privacy policy, access

00:12:01.683 --> 00:12:04.220
controls, recipients, retention and

00:12:04.281 --> 00:12:05.544
backups.

00:12:06.315 --> 00:12:09.702
The service uses authentication cookies,

00:12:09.766 --> 00:12:13.401
including lw_session for signed-in members

00:12:13.493 --> 00:12:16.509
and lw_guest for guest access where

00:12:16.568 --> 00:12:17.819
enabled.

00:12:18.602 --> 00:12:21.522
These are separate from the CA enrolment

00:12:21.585 --> 00:12:23.144
cookie below.

00:12:23.897 --> 00:12:26.560
Policy refreshes and enabled usage

00:12:26.605 --> 00:12:29.645
reporting can make requests while the app

00:12:29.725 --> 00:12:33.029
is in use; a separate click is not needed

00:12:33.129 --> 00:12:35.170
for every request.

00:12:35.937 --> 00:12:38.304
This is traffic to the configured

00:12:38.369 --> 00:12:41.454
instance, not a report to the Lolly

00:12:41.516 --> 00:12:43.987
project about deployments it does not

00:12:44.046 --> 00:12:45.294
operate.

00:12:46.088 --> 00:12:49.085
Usage telemetry has three levels: off

00:12:49.142 --> 00:12:52.130
stores no usage events; aggregate strips

00:12:52.194 --> 00:12:56.319
user ids; standard can attribute events.

00:12:57.089 --> 00:13:00.618
The default attribution policy is opt-in,

00:13:00.678 --> 00:13:03.371
which requires the user's consent before

00:13:03.439 --> 00:13:05.869
storing a user id.

00:13:06.642 --> 00:13:09.215
An operator can instead configure

00:13:09.295 --> 00:13:10.979
attributed reporting with

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:14.294
telemetryAttribution: default.

00:13:15.084 --> 00:13:17.969
Allowed attributes are labels, not tool

00:13:18.029 --> 00:13:19.719
input values.

00:13:20.525 --> 00:13:23.393
See the telemetry reference.

00:13:24.187 --> 00:13:26.468
Audit is separate.

00:13:27.248 --> 00:13:30.708
Governed actions can retain an identified

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:34.168
audit record regardless of usage-telemetry

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:35.544
consent.

00:13:36.303 --> 00:13:38.841
Turning telemetry off does not turn off

00:13:38.927 --> 00:13:42.108
shared-session storage, approval records,

00:13:42.181 --> 00:13:44.745
render-job storage or audit.

00:13:45.524 --> 00:13:48.234
The operator controls retention and

00:13:48.296 --> 00:13:50.807
erasure, including any audit

00:13:50.898 --> 00:13:54.969
pseudonymisation; see data lifecycle.

00:13:55.753 --> 00:13:59.494
Local deletion is not server deletion.

00:14:00.276 --> 00:14:02.752
Leaving an instance or clearing your

00:14:02.813 --> 00:14:05.811
browser removes local state, not the

00:14:05.882 --> 00:14:09.444
organisation's stored records or backups.

00:14:10.215 --> 00:14:13.421
Ask the operator for access, export or

00:14:13.481 --> 00:14:16.145
erasure of server-held data.

00:14:16.900 --> 00:14:19.944
Personal Sync and Export my data are

00:14:20.006 --> 00:14:22.991
backups of your device, not of that

00:14:23.053 --> 00:14:25.294
organisation service.

00:14:26.057 --> 00:14:28.675
The public lolly-work sandbox is a

00:14:28.737 --> 00:14:32.046
demonstration with memory-only state, not

00:14:32.135 --> 00:14:34.820
durable storage for your work.

00:14:35.953 --> 00:14:38.305
Hot-linked render URL'S

00:14:39.298 --> 00:14:41.843
Live on lolly-tools.

00:14:42.625 --> 00:14:44.868
Every lolly-tools>.

00:14:45.641 --> 00:14:45.715
?

00:14:46.515 --> 00:14:49.590
URL renders for real, and the inputs

00:14:49.652 --> 00:14:51.919
travel in that URL.

00:14:52.681 --> 00:14:55.356
The section below is what that means for

00:14:55.446 --> 00:14:58.316
you, and an operator can switch the

00:14:58.405 --> 00:15:01.145
feature off on their own instance.

00:15:01.925 --> 00:15:04.936
The app itself stays entirely on your

00:15:04.998 --> 00:15:06.244
device.

00:15:07.035 --> 00:15:09.564
Separately, an operator can enable

00:15:09.655 --> 00:15:13.269
hot-link render URL'S - /tool/ .

00:15:14.041 --> 00:15:14.115
?

00:15:14.864 --> 00:15:17.742
- so a shared Lolly link can appear as a

00:15:17.803 --> 00:15:20.988
live image in a README, a wiki or a

00:15:21.049 --> 00:15:22.394
dashboard.

00:15:23.164 --> 00:15:25.842
Fetching one asks the server to render

00:15:25.902 --> 00:15:29.046
public tool and catalogue data with the

00:15:29.117 --> 00:15:32.070
inputs written into the URL.

00:15:32.866 --> 00:15:36.094
No accounts, no cookies, no state.

00:15:36.876 --> 00:15:40.414
The endpoint is anonymous, and nothing

00:15:41.311 --> 00:15:44.193
on your device is read.

00:15:44.977 --> 00:15:48.141
Your documents, sessions and uploads never

00:15:48.202 --> 00:15:50.704
leave your browser - they cannot appear in

00:15:50.765 --> 00:15:52.619
these links at all.

00:15:53.387 --> 00:15:57.094
But the URL itself is recorded.

00:15:57.861 --> 00:16:00.585
A URL'S query string is part of the

00:16:00.642 --> 00:16:01.690
request

00:16:02.725 --> 00:16:05.212
line, so it shows up in the hosting

00:16:05.274 --> 00:16:08.635
platform's ordinary access logs the same

00:16:08.697 --> 00:16:11.669
way every requested path does.

00:16:12.425 --> 00:16:15.170
If a link's inputs contain someone's name

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:18.427
or email - a name badge, an email

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:21.774
signature - that text sits in those logs,

00:16:21.834 --> 00:16:24.532
and no amount of policy wording changes

00:16:24.593 --> 00:16:25.519
it.

00:16:26.318 --> 00:16:29.758
So a hot-link URL is the wrong place for

00:16:29.820 --> 00:16:33.022
personal details: give it only what you

00:16:33.074 --> 00:16:35.569
would put on a public page.

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:38.948
The inputs are public by construction

00:16:39.047 --> 00:16:41.869
anyway - they are whatever the link's

00:16:42.816 --> 00:16:46.074
author typed into the URL, readable by

00:16:46.163 --> 00:16:48.569
anyone the link reaches.

00:16:49.344 --> 00:16:52.643
Don't put secrets in a shared link.

00:16:53.448 --> 00:16:56.735
Lolly offers link encryption for sensitive

00:16:56.798 --> 00:16:58.144
content.

00:16:58.925 --> 00:17:01.954
Responses are cached and rate-limited like

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:04.876
any public image, and marked

00:17:05.882 --> 00:17:09.144
noindex so search engines don't index your

00:17:09.205 --> 00:17:10.394
renders.

00:17:11.181 --> 00:17:14.215
Self-hosting Lolly and don't want a public

00:17:14.276 --> 00:17:15.944
render surface?

00:17:16.725 --> 00:17:20.510
Set LOLLY_DISABLE_RENDER_GET=1 and every

00:17:20.571 --> 00:17:24.595
one of these URL'S returns 404.

00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:30.052
The MCP server «optional, for AI agents»

00:17:31.019 --> 00:17:34.453
Lolly can also be reached by an AI agent

00:17:34.523 --> 00:17:37.409
over the Model Context Protocol - an

00:17:37.494 --> 00:17:40.146
operator-run endpoint «lolly-tools runs

00:17:40.214 --> 00:17:43.687
one; anyone can self-host their own,

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:46.144
including fully air-gapped».

00:17:46.902 --> 00:17:49.555
It shares the render path's no-accounts

00:17:49.618 --> 00:17:52.861
posture, plus four tools that necessarily

00:17:52.924 --> 00:17:54.919
handle file bytes:

00:17:55.706 --> 00:17:58.835
lolly_transform «run an on-device utility

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:01.427
server-side, on the calling

00:18:02.303 --> 00:18:04.949
agent's behalf», lolly_verify «check

00:18:05.010 --> 00:18:07.925
Content Credentials» and lolly_redact

00:18:07.985 --> 00:18:11.608
«black out regions of an image or PDF» all

00:18:11.665 --> 00:18:14.895
accept a file's bytes from the caller.

00:18:15.657 --> 00:18:18.884
They are processed in-process, in memory,

00:18:18.947 --> 00:18:21.581
and the result is returned in that same

00:18:21.652 --> 00:18:24.703
call - the file is never written to disk

00:18:24.788 --> 00:18:26.797
and never stored once the request

00:18:26.857 --> 00:18:28.095
completes.

00:18:28.897 --> 00:18:32.269
lolly_rebrand «renovate an old slide deck

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:34.593
onto a design system,

00:18:35.354 --> 00:18:38.130
across its plan, compile and inspect

00:18:38.183 --> 00:18:40.955
stages» accepts a deck's bytes the same

00:18:41.015 --> 00:18:44.426
way, and processes them in memory, for

00:18:44.475 --> 00:18:46.786
that call only - nothing is written to

00:18:46.854 --> 00:18:50.345
disk or kept once the response is sent.

00:18:51.091 --> 00:18:54.096
Its first stage, capabilities, states in

00:18:54.157 --> 00:18:56.451
words where your bytes would go before you

00:18:56.525 --> 00:18:59.941
send any: on a self-hosted local server

00:19:00.009 --> 00:19:02.942
the deck never leaves that machine; on a

00:19:03.003 --> 00:19:05.799
hosted server, calling lolly_rebrand sends

00:19:05.841 --> 00:19:08.815
the deck there, up to the size and slide

00:19:08.875 --> 00:19:11.520
limits that same stage gives.

00:19:12.272 --> 00:19:14.208
Every other tool - lolly_render,

00:19:14.272 --> 00:19:17.420
lolly_build_url, lolly_list_tools,

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:20.192
lolly_describe_tool - works from

00:19:20.252 --> 00:19:23.662
parameters only «text, numbers, colours,

00:19:23.741 --> 00:19:26.905
URL'S, catalogue asset ids», the same

00:19:26.965 --> 00:19:30.395
inputs a hot-link render URL takes.

00:19:31.153 --> 00:19:33.617
Access is either a shared token the

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:36.532
operator issues to clients they trust, or

00:19:37.553 --> 00:19:40.917
stateless OAuth 2 point 1: short-lived

00:19:41.001 --> 00:19:43.690
signed tokens verified against a shared

00:19:43.776 --> 00:19:46.968
secret, nothing stored server-side and the

00:19:47.034 --> 00:19:50.136
token itself is never written to a log or

00:19:50.189 --> 00:19:52.220
a render URL.

00:19:53.323 --> 00:19:56.502
Content Credentials identity «a sign-in

00:19:56.549 --> 00:19:58.763
you have to start yourself»

00:19:59.742 --> 00:20:02.479
Lolly can seal a cryptographic Content

00:20:02.541 --> 00:20:05.866
Credential into your exports so anyone can

00:20:05.927 --> 00:20:09.751
verify, offline, that a file is unaltered

00:20:09.814 --> 00:20:11.769
since it left Lolly.

00:20:12.535 --> 00:20:15.895
That much is on by default and fully local

00:20:15.977 --> 00:20:18.669
- the signing key is generated on your

00:20:18.729 --> 00:20:22.495
device and signing itself happens offline.

00:20:23.254 --> 00:20:26.582
Without enrolment that key is a throwaway:

00:20:26.641 --> 00:20:29.640
a fresh keypair minted for each export and

00:20:29.705 --> 00:20:31.294
dropped with it.

00:20:32.062 --> 00:20:35.123
Once you enrol, the key becomes a lasting

00:20:35.183 --> 00:20:38.334
one and is generated non-extractable - not

00:20:38.394 --> 00:20:41.675
even Lolly's own code can read it, only

00:20:41.747 --> 00:20:43.695
ask it to sign.

00:20:44.485 --> 00:20:48.168
Either way it never leaves your device.

00:20:48.941 --> 00:20:51.585
This section covers the one optional step

00:20:51.628 --> 00:20:54.854
on top of that: enrolling a verified

00:20:54.916 --> 00:20:58.419
identity, so your exports say "Verified -

00:20:58.483 --> 00:21:03.119
signed by \ " instead of an anonymous key.

00:21:03.874 --> 00:21:06.651
If you skip enrolment, this certificate

00:21:06.735 --> 00:21:09.610
service receives no enrolment data from

00:21:09.686 --> 00:21:10.644
you.

00:21:11.416 --> 00:21:14.218
Other optional services have the data

00:21:14.316 --> 00:21:16.619
flows described above.

00:21:17.387 --> 00:21:20.385
If you do enrol, here is exactly what

00:21:20.448 --> 00:21:21.718
happens:

00:21:22.502 --> 00:21:24.991
You choose a sign-in method - GitHub,

00:21:25.054 --> 00:21:27.882
Google, SUSE «id-suse-com» or an

00:21:28.901 --> 00:21:30.769
emailed link.

00:21:31.551 --> 00:21:34.082
For the three OIDC providers, you're

00:21:34.147 --> 00:21:37.036
redirected to that provider's own login

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:40.179
page, governed by their privacy policy,

00:21:40.237 --> 00:21:41.744
not ours.

00:21:42.533 --> 00:21:45.254
Lolly's certificate service receives back

00:21:45.351 --> 00:21:48.394
only a verified email address and the

00:21:48.455 --> 00:21:50.145
provider's name.

00:21:50.923 --> 00:21:53.441
For the email link, the address you type

00:21:53.485 --> 00:21:56.856
is passed to Resend, a transactional email

00:21:56.918 --> 00:22:00.594
API, solely to deliver that one link.

00:22:01.374 --> 00:22:03.857
A short-lived cookie protects the

00:22:03.923 --> 00:22:05.443
redirect.

00:22:06.209 --> 00:22:07.938
The certificate service sets

00:22:08.015 --> 00:22:11.841
lolly_ca_state, HttpOnly, scoped to

00:22:11.931 --> 00:22:14.544
/api/ca,

00:22:15.324 --> 00:22:18.119
expiring within ten minutes.

00:22:18.863 --> 00:22:21.884
It carries a random value, not a tracking

00:22:21.943 --> 00:22:25.243
identifier, and exists only to stop the

00:22:25.317 --> 00:22:28.270
OAuth redirect being forged.

00:22:29.031 --> 00:22:31.643
It is cleared as soon as sign-in

00:22:31.706 --> 00:22:32.968
completes.

00:22:33.757 --> 00:22:36.855
Your IP address is used, briefly, to

00:22:36.916 --> 00:22:39.261
prevent abuse of the sign-in

00:22:40.273 --> 00:22:42.970
endpoints «so one script can't spam an

00:22:43.032 --> 00:22:46.419
inbox or exhaust the email quota».

00:22:47.213 --> 00:22:49.634
Lolly hashes it before creating a

00:22:49.780 --> 00:22:52.806
short-lived abuse-control bucket; the raw

00:22:52.867 --> 00:22:56.019
address is not sent to that store.

00:22:56.794 --> 00:22:59.777
The bucket expires after about a minute

00:22:59.858 --> 00:23:02.719
and is not used for tracking.

00:23:03.489 --> 00:23:06.643
Ordinary hosting access logs are separate

00:23:06.731 --> 00:23:08.919
and described below.

00:23:09.687 --> 00:23:11.804
The certificate service issues a

00:23:11.932 --> 00:23:15.618
short-lived certificate «7, 30, 90 or

00:23:15.715 --> 00:23:17.945
365

00:23:18.943 --> 00:23:21.495
days, your choice, capped by the

00:23:21.572 --> 00:23:24.623
operator's policy» binding your verified

00:23:24.687 --> 00:23:27.516
email to the public half of the keypair

00:23:27.625 --> 00:23:30.145
generated on your device.

00:23:30.921 --> 00:23:33.307
The private half never leaves your

00:23:33.371 --> 00:23:34.668
browser.

00:23:35.482 --> 00:23:39.218
Nothing about the issuance is recorded.

00:23:40.004 --> 00:23:43.039
The certificate service keeps no

00:23:43.971 --> 00:23:46.507
issuance log: not your email, not the

00:23:46.568 --> 00:23:49.125
provider, not a serial number, not a

00:23:49.185 --> 00:23:50.595
timestamp.

00:23:51.396 --> 00:23:55.143
No database, no log line, no webhook.

00:23:55.949 --> 00:23:59.240
Your email address exists in the request

00:23:59.361 --> 00:24:01.924
only long enough to be written into the

00:24:01.988 --> 00:24:05.542
certificate that your own device receives,

00:24:05.605 --> 00:24:08.224
and then it is gone from our side

00:24:08.292 --> 00:24:09.744
entirely.

00:24:10.509 --> 00:24:13.493
After that, signing is offline again for

00:24:13.553 --> 00:24:16.319
the certificate's whole lifetime.

00:24:17.093 --> 00:24:19.738
Exporting a file never contacts the

00:24:19.800 --> 00:24:23.644
certificate service - only enrolling did.

00:24:24.428 --> 00:24:27.418
The tradeoff, stated plainly.

00:24:28.192 --> 00:24:31.327
An earlier version of this service did log

00:24:31.400 --> 00:24:34.317
each issuance, so that a misissued or

00:24:34.391 --> 00:24:37.470
compromised certificate could be traced.

00:24:38.260 --> 00:24:41.686
We removed it to avoid retaining personal

00:24:41.748 --> 00:24:44.744
data in this certificate service.

00:24:45.514 --> 00:24:49.241
Organisation identity and audit records in

00:24:49.304 --> 00:24:52.233
lolly-work are separate and follow the

00:24:52.327 --> 00:24:55.019
operator's retention policy.

00:24:55.796 --> 00:24:57.798
What we give up is server-side

00:24:57.860 --> 00:25:01.565
traceability: if a certificate is misused

00:25:01.629 --> 00:25:04.644
we cannot look up who obtained it.

00:25:05.420 --> 00:25:08.402
Certificates are short-lived by design - 7

00:25:08.491 --> 00:25:13.313
to 365 days, your choice, capped by the

00:25:13.375 --> 00:25:16.596
operator - and expire on their own, which

00:25:16.658 --> 00:25:20.095
is the mitigation we rely on instead.

00:25:20.878 --> 00:25:23.942
Self-hosters whose own obligations require

00:25:24.042 --> 00:25:27.612
an audit log can add one, and become the

00:25:27.672 --> 00:25:31.020
controller of that data by doing so.

00:25:32.159 --> 00:25:34.518
The browser extension

00:25:35.453 --> 00:25:38.869
The Lolly URL Screenshot browser extension

00:25:38.940 --> 00:25:42.161
does not collect, store or transmit any

00:25:42.224 --> 00:25:43.993
personal data.

00:25:44.783 --> 00:25:47.567
No analytics, no tracking, no remote

00:25:47.659 --> 00:25:48.769
server.

00:25:49.554 --> 00:25:51.268
What it does.

00:25:52.043 --> 00:25:54.121
When you ask the Lolly web app to

00:25:54.197 --> 00:25:58.224
screenshot a URL, the extension opens that

00:25:58.310 --> 00:26:01.057
page in a temporary background tab,

00:26:01.132 --> 00:26:03.632
captures it in your browser using the

00:26:03.697 --> 00:26:07.196
DevTools Protocol, hands the image back to

00:26:07.257 --> 00:26:09.919
the app and closes the tab.

00:26:10.687 --> 00:26:13.534
Everything happens locally, on your own

00:26:13.594 --> 00:26:15.644
device and network.

00:26:16.430 --> 00:26:17.686
Data.

00:26:18.489 --> 00:26:20.668
We collect nothing.

00:26:21.449 --> 00:26:24.655
The extension has no servers and makes no

00:26:24.718 --> 00:26:25.689
network

00:26:26.700 --> 00:26:29.219
requests of its own.

00:26:29.970 --> 00:26:32.636
Captured images go straight to the Lolly

00:26:32.708 --> 00:26:35.179
app in the same browser - never

00:26:36.284 --> 00:26:39.292
uploaded by the extension.

00:26:40.063 --> 00:26:42.819
The URL'S you capture are used only to

00:26:42.881 --> 00:26:45.616
load that one page for that one

00:26:46.552 --> 00:26:47.991
screenshot.

00:26:48.780 --> 00:26:51.817
They are not logged or shared.

00:26:52.589 --> 00:26:54.143
Permissions.

00:26:54.915 --> 00:26:57.725
debugger - to capture the rendered page

00:26:57.795 --> 00:27:00.513
via the DevTools Protocol «the

00:27:01.517 --> 00:27:04.499
same mechanism the Lolly desktop app

00:27:04.562 --> 00:27:05.743
uses».

00:27:06.508 --> 00:27:09.629
tabs - to open and close the temporary tab

00:27:09.690 --> 00:27:11.644
the page loads in.

00:27:12.408 --> 00:27:14.790
Host access « » - because the page you

00:27:14.851 --> 00:27:17.140
choose to capture can be

00:27:17.962 --> 00:27:19.845
on any site.

00:27:20.612 --> 00:27:24.208
Chrome surfaces this at install time as a

00:27:24.300 --> 00:27:26.444
broad permission warning.

00:27:27.225 --> 00:27:30.925
The extension only ever visits the URL you

00:27:30.988 --> 00:27:32.193
give it.

00:27:33.001 --> 00:27:36.478
None of these are used to read, monitor or

00:27:36.540 --> 00:27:39.103
transmit your browsing beyond that one

00:27:39.164 --> 00:27:41.069
requested capture.

00:27:42.199 --> 00:27:44.371
Infrastructure logs

00:27:45.381 --> 00:27:47.879
This section describes the public

00:27:47.944 --> 00:27:50.292
lolly-tools deployment.

00:27:51.049 --> 00:27:53.688
Its hosting platform records ordinary

00:27:53.747 --> 00:27:57.539
request metadata: IP address, requested

00:27:57.619 --> 00:28:00.769
path, timestamp and user agent.

00:28:01.565 --> 00:28:05.043
Local edits do not reach that host.

00:28:05.810 --> 00:28:08.381
A hot-link render's query string can

00:28:08.443 --> 00:28:11.618
contain the text supplied by its caller,

00:28:11.695 --> 00:28:13.819
as explained above.

00:28:14.596 --> 00:28:18.333
MCP file tools process supplied bytes in

00:28:18.396 --> 00:28:19.519
memory.

00:28:20.286 --> 00:28:22.631
A separate lolly-work deployment

00:28:22.752 --> 00:28:25.254
additionally holds the service records

00:28:25.315 --> 00:28:28.514
described above and has its operator's

00:28:28.610 --> 00:28:30.294
logging policy.

00:28:31.079 --> 00:28:34.382
The public services minimise application

00:28:34.446 --> 00:28:35.618
logging.

00:28:36.399 --> 00:28:39.704
The MCP server contains no logging

00:28:39.769 --> 00:28:41.693
statements at all.

00:28:42.460 --> 00:28:45.198
The certificate service emits exactly two

00:28:45.259 --> 00:28:48.043
lines, both on failure and both

00:28:48.112 --> 00:28:50.873
deliberately stripped: a send-failure

00:28:50.934 --> 00:28:54.306
status code with no recipient address, and

00:28:54.371 --> 00:28:56.948
an error message with no stack trace or

00:28:57.017 --> 00:28:59.977
URL «a stack could carry an enrolment

00:29:00.038 --> 00:29:01.219
token».

00:29:01.984 --> 00:29:04.742
Everything else in the log is the hosting

00:29:04.803 --> 00:29:07.144
platform's, not ours.

00:29:07.936 --> 00:29:11.010
For lolly-tools, hosting is Vercel and

00:29:11.091 --> 00:29:14.323
access-log retention follows Vercel's own

00:29:14.386 --> 00:29:17.468
platform defaults for our plan.

00:29:18.244 --> 00:29:21.506
We configure no log drain, no long-term

00:29:21.566 --> 00:29:24.530
log export and no analytics or monitoring

00:29:24.591 --> 00:29:26.320
product on top.

00:29:27.071 --> 00:29:30.214
We keep no copy of these logs ourselves,

00:29:30.269 --> 00:29:33.092
which also means we have no way to search

00:29:33.150 --> 00:29:35.596
them for you - see Your rights.

00:29:36.741 --> 00:29:40.269
Legal bases, retention and recipients

00:29:41.207 --> 00:29:43.587
This table covers the reference

00:29:43.702 --> 00:29:46.117
lolly-tools deployment.

00:29:46.870 --> 00:29:49.519
It does not state the legal bases or

00:29:49.578 --> 00:29:52.730
retention periods of your organisation's

00:29:52.879 --> 00:29:56.175
lolly-work instance; its operator must

00:29:56.236 --> 00:29:59.244
provide those in its own policy.

00:30:00.032 --> 00:30:01.693
Recipients.

00:30:02.472 --> 00:30:05.494
The categories of recipient are: our

00:30:05.557 --> 00:30:08.243
hosting provider «Vercel Inc.»

00:30:08.971 --> 00:30:11.831
; our abuse-control store provider, which

00:30:11.882 --> 00:30:14.822
receives only short-lived, one-way-derived

00:30:14.883 --> 00:30:18.685
bucket keys and never the raw IP address;

00:30:18.753 --> 00:30:21.504
and - only if you use the email sign-in

00:30:21.565 --> 00:30:24.580
option - a transactional email provider

00:30:24.641 --> 00:30:25.895
«Resend».

00:30:26.650 --> 00:30:30.167
If you sign in with GitHub, Google or SUSE

00:30:30.252 --> 00:30:33.280
«id-suse-com», you interact with that

00:30:33.340 --> 00:30:36.022
provider directly under their own privacy

00:30:36.083 --> 00:30:37.295
policy.

00:30:38.055 --> 00:30:41.375
They tell us a verified email address and

00:30:41.437 --> 00:30:42.869
nothing else.

00:30:43.648 --> 00:30:46.802
We share personal data with no one else,

00:30:46.862 --> 00:30:50.112
and we do not sell data, run advertising

00:30:50.160 --> 00:30:52.194
or profile users.

00:30:52.960 --> 00:30:55.993
Transfers outside the EEA.

00:30:56.788 --> 00:31:00.718
Vercel and Resend are US companies.

00:31:01.497 --> 00:31:04.226
Function compute for lolly-tools is pinned

00:31:04.321 --> 00:31:07.329
to Vercel's Frankfurt «fra1» region so

00:31:07.391 --> 00:31:10.783
processing happens in the EU, but as

00:31:10.845 --> 00:31:13.534
US-headquartered providers they may still

00:31:13.624 --> 00:31:17.619
access data as processors from the US.

00:31:18.395 --> 00:31:21.129
Those transfers rely on the European

00:31:21.189 --> 00:31:24.153
Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses

00:31:24.238 --> 00:31:28.763
and/or the EU-US Data Privacy Framework,

00:31:28.837 --> 00:31:31.334
as set out in each provider's data

00:31:31.395 --> 00:31:33.295
processing agreement.

00:31:34.048 --> 00:31:36.342
Because the personal data reaching these

00:31:36.402 --> 00:31:39.683
providers is so limited - an email address

00:31:39.756 --> 00:31:42.326
passed through to send one message,

00:31:42.394 --> 00:31:45.637
ordinary access logs, and a short-lived

00:31:45.697 --> 00:31:48.093
derived abuse-control bucket - the

00:31:48.173 --> 00:31:51.445
exposure is correspondingly small.

00:31:52.228 --> 00:31:55.243
Automated decision-making.

00:31:56.056 --> 00:31:57.064
None.

00:31:57.840 --> 00:32:00.946
There is no profiling and no automated

00:32:01.006 --> 00:32:03.955
decision producing legal or similarly

00:32:04.038 --> 00:32:06.394
significant effects «Art.

00:32:07.143 --> 00:32:08.867
22».

00:32:09.988 --> 00:32:11.995
Children's privacy

00:32:12.988 --> 00:32:15.716
Ordinary local app use does not send

00:32:15.784 --> 00:32:18.819
personal content to lolly-tools.

00:32:19.562 --> 00:32:22.409
Its optional Content Credentials enrolment

00:32:22.475 --> 00:32:25.679
receives an email address and is not

00:32:25.738 --> 00:32:29.145
directed at or intended for children.

00:32:29.909 --> 00:32:32.486
Organisation services have separate

00:32:32.542 --> 00:32:34.983
accounts and data handling; their

00:32:35.054 --> 00:32:37.619
operator's policy applies.

00:32:38.764 --> 00:32:39.942
Your rights

00:32:40.816 --> 00:32:43.908
For records stored only on your device,

00:32:43.967 --> 00:32:46.731
you can access, correct, delete and move

00:32:46.783 --> 00:32:48.670
the data yourself.

00:32:49.459 --> 00:32:52.635
Your data lives in your browser's storage,

00:32:52.695 --> 00:32:55.848
in a form you can inspect, export «Export

00:32:55.893 --> 00:32:59.069
my data, above» or delete «by clearing the

00:32:59.161 --> 00:33:02.745
site's storage in your browser, as above».

00:33:03.512 --> 00:33:07.352
Formally, under GDPR Articles 15 to 22 you

00:33:07.400 --> 00:33:09.499
have the right to access your personal

00:33:09.559 --> 00:33:13.264
data, to rectify it, to erase it, to

00:33:13.316 --> 00:33:15.506
restrict or object to its processing

00:33:15.563 --> 00:33:17.971
«including objecting to anything we base

00:33:18.004 --> 00:33:20.395
on legitimate interests», to data

00:33:20.455 --> 00:33:22.735
portability and - where processing rests

00:33:22.785 --> 00:33:25.194
on consent - to withdraw that consent at

00:33:25.249 --> 00:33:28.127
any time, without affecting the lawfulness

00:33:28.170 --> 00:33:31.095
of what happened before you withdrew it.

00:33:31.865 --> 00:33:34.154
For the public lolly-tools services

00:33:34.213 --> 00:33:36.944
described here, we no longer keep an

00:33:37.011 --> 00:33:40.304
issuance log, so we hold no personal data

00:33:40.351 --> 00:33:43.024
about you that we can look up, correct,

00:33:43.095 --> 00:33:45.045
export or delete.

00:33:45.788 --> 00:33:48.398
If you write and ask what we have on you,

00:33:48.456 --> 00:33:51.073
the truthful answer is nothing, and we

00:33:51.132 --> 00:33:52.695
will state it.

00:33:53.471 --> 00:33:56.645
The one category that exists at all is

00:33:56.707 --> 00:33:59.827
hosting access logs keyed to an IP

00:33:59.887 --> 00:34:03.053
address, held by our hosting provider

00:34:03.129 --> 00:34:05.719
under their retention defaults.

00:34:06.487 --> 00:34:08.949
We have no facility to search or

00:34:09.040 --> 00:34:12.310
selectively delete those, and we will tell

00:34:12.400 --> 00:34:15.544
you that rather than pretend otherwise.

00:34:16.342 --> 00:34:19.535
Your local records remain accessible on

00:34:19.602 --> 00:34:21.143
your device.

00:34:21.932 --> 00:34:25.370
For organisation-held work, identities,

00:34:25.432 --> 00:34:28.772
telemetry and audit records, contact your

00:34:28.835 --> 00:34:32.018
lolly-work operator; local export and

00:34:32.056 --> 00:34:34.546
deletion controls do not manage those

00:34:34.607 --> 00:34:35.794
copies.

00:34:36.587 --> 00:34:39.618
You have the right to complain.

00:34:40.377 --> 00:34:42.627
If you think we have handled your data

00:34:42.688 --> 00:34:45.878
improperly, you can lodge a complaint with

00:34:45.938 --> 00:34:49.130
a data protection supervisory authority -

00:34:49.188 --> 00:34:52.609
in the EU, the authority in your country

00:34:52.650 --> 00:34:55.562
of residence, place of work or where you

00:34:55.620 --> 00:34:58.545
believe the infringement occurred «Art.

00:34:59.326 --> 00:35:01.244
77».

00:35:02.019 --> 00:35:04.934
Our lead supervisory authority is the

00:35:05.023 --> 00:35:06.929
Bayerisches Landesamt für

00:35:07.007 --> 00:35:10.273
Datenschutzaufsicht «BayLDA» in Ansbach,

00:35:10.334 --> 00:35:11.545
Germany.

00:35:12.321 --> 00:35:15.153
You do not need to contact us first,

00:35:15.213 --> 00:35:18.419
though we would like the chance to fix it.

00:35:19.208 --> 00:35:22.343
We do not sell personal data.

00:35:23.457 --> 00:35:26.030
Changes to this policy

00:35:26.988 --> 00:35:29.960
The date at the top changes whenever this

00:35:30.027 --> 00:35:31.694
document does.

00:35:32.461 --> 00:35:34.831
A change that alters what leaves your

00:35:34.890 --> 00:35:37.705
device or what's retained gets its own

00:35:37.766 --> 00:35:41.191
line here, not a silent edit - if you want

00:35:41.273 --> 00:35:44.218
to see what changed, ask «below» or

00:35:44.279 --> 00:35:47.044
compare against the public source.

00:35:47.813 --> 00:35:52.641
29 September 20 26: clarified the optional

00:35:52.702 --> 00:35:56.106
lolly-work service, its organisation-held

00:35:56.169 --> 00:35:59.408
content, authentication cookies, usage

00:35:59.469 --> 00:36:02.202
telemetry and audit records, and the

00:36:02.291 --> 00:36:04.866
separation between local deletion and

00:36:04.961 --> 00:36:06.744
server retention.

00:36:07.526 --> 00:36:10.862
These are existing optional workflows, not

00:36:10.913 --> 00:36:13.376
a new upload requirement for local

00:36:13.438 --> 00:36:14.644
editing.

